{
  "name": "Forecast list",
  "description": "Six hours laid out across a tile: the time, the condition icon and the temperature, one cell per hour. `direction: across` makes the cells run left to right and `columns` is not read at all, a row across being one line by definition. The icon is never on the wire: each side maps `condition` to its own glyph from the same table, so a drift fails a test rather than showing a different picture on the watch than in the editor. Twenty-four hours were found and six are drawn, which is what `total` records.",
